WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.310
It wasn't that long ago that Keanu Reeves
made his first appearance as headshot-happy,

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.929
dog-loving hitman John Wick in the critically
acclaimed film of the same name.

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:14.469
In the years since, though the world of assassins
and gold coins that he lives in has grown

00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:18.050
considerably, and will be expanding a whole
lot more in the near future.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:22.710
There's already a line of comic books slowly
revealing more about Wick's shadowy past,

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.089
and a TV spinoff is currently in the pipeline
at Starz.

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:30.279
Both are exciting projects, but it's Reeves'
third outing as the steely anti-hero that

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:32.070
everyone's really waiting for.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.190
From returning characters and exotic filming
locations to production schedules and release

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:40.010
dates, this is everything we know about John
Wick: Chapter 3.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.210
The band’s back together

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:47.000
The biggest obstacle for John Wick: Chapter
3 was always going to be convincing Keanu

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.199
Reeves to reprise his role.

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:53.399
As he found out with the Matrix trilogy, third
time isn't always a charm.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:57.609
Luckily for Wick fans, Reeves was expressing
his interest in a third film before the second

00:00:57.609 --> 00:00:58.940
one was even released.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.609
In February 2018, Reeves said that he was
"absolutely" on board for John Wick: Chapter

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:08.410
3, telling Entertainment Weekly that he loves
the character and the world, and that if audiences

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.650
were into what he did in the sequel, he’d
have the chance to continue.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.010
It turns out they did.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:18.330
Chapter 2 racked up an 89% Fresh rating on
Rotten Tomatoes, and Reeves got his wish,

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:22.030
with Chapter 3 being set for release in summer
2019.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:26.880
Writer Derek Kolstad came aboard in summer
2017, and Chad Stahelski, who co-directed

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.130
and directed John Wick and Chapter 2, respectively,
is back on board, too.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.140
Familiar faces

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.850
With John Wick’s success, it’s no surprise
that producers have been spending a whole

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.630
lot of time figuring out how to continue the
character’s story.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.960
When Chad Stahelski was asked for more details,
he revealed that Chapter 3 is going to bring

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:48.440
a few characters from the periphery of the
action into the spotlight.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:53.030
Stahelski has mentioned that Ian McShane and
Lance Reddick will both be back in prominent

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:57.510
roles, meaning that the Continental, a hotel
that caters to working assassins, will likely

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.410
play a key role in the film.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:03.420
Wick was excommunicated from the hotel for
conducting business on its grounds in Chapter

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.530
2, but judging from these early comments,
it looks like he’s not done with the secretive

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.539
underworld establishment just yet.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:13.970
Common, Laurence Fishburne, and Ruby Rose
are all preparing to reprise their roles as

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:14.970
well.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.860
The last time we saw Rose's character, the
mute assassin Ares, she was bleeding out in

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.829
a hall of mirrors after making the mistake
of fighting John Wick.

00:02:22.829 --> 00:02:25.140
Apparently it’ll take more than that to
stop her.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.370
On the road

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:31.269
While John Wick was set entirely in New York,
Chapter 2 took him to the gloriously cinematic

00:02:31.269 --> 00:02:35.629
city of Rome, and it looks as though he'll
be getting at least one new stamp in his passport

00:02:35.629 --> 00:02:36.719
in part three.

00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:41.530
According to Stahelski's interview with Digital
Spy, the plan is to keep Wick on the move,

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.079
and numerous destinations have already been
tossed around behind closed doors.

00:02:45.079 --> 00:02:46.140
Stahelski said,

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:50.980
"We talked about the UK, Paris, we'd love
to do the Middle East and Asia."

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:56.010
Reeves even told IGN that he’d like to see
John in Jerusalem, sending him into the desert

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.569
in an effort to go somewhere with a history
that goes beyond even Rome’s.

00:02:59.569 --> 00:03:03.879
It ultimately falls to writer Derek Kolstad
to shape Wick's journey, and his choice is

00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:06.200
Tokyo, who told the Jeff Goldsmith Podcast,

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.239
"One of the things I would love John to do
in the third one is to be excommunicated,

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:14.920
broke, begging, in Tokyo or some corner of
the Earth that’s sexy and cool."

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:20.209
Taking the story to Japan might help to underline
Wick’s status as a sort of modern-day ronin,

00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:24.050
and recent reports suggest that this might
just be what the producers are going for.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:29.409
Hiroyuki Sanada, who formed a friendship with
Reeves on the set of the samurai flop 47 Ronin,

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:34.879
has apparently joined the cast as the central
antagonist: the boss of a Japanese crime syndicate.

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:36.490
Pull up a chair to the High Table

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:42.359
While 2014's John Wick was a straight-up revenge
flick, the 2017 sequel fleshed out the mysterious

00:03:42.359 --> 00:03:46.529
world of professional killers considerably,
revealing the existence of an all-powerful

00:03:46.529 --> 00:03:50.360
council of assassins and crime lords known
as "The High Table."

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.800
“The Camorras doubled Santino's open contract,
it's gone international."

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.120
“High table?”

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.240
According to Kolstad,

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:02.430
"In one of the early script drafts we went
in-depth on what the High Table is until we

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.569
realized it was too much for one story."

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:09.840
Luckily, Kolstad's interview seemed to indicate
that Chapter 3 will finally go for it, which

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.049
was then confirmed by the director.

00:04:12.049 --> 00:04:16.380
Reeves also teased the High Table's involvement
in Chapter 3 during an interview with Empire,

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.380
saying,

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:18.910
"Maybe the High Table shows up.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.170
And then the High Table starts firing guns.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:25.000
And then maybe this kind of thing starts to
happen between the High Table and Continental?"

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.840
Wouldn’t that be awesome?

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:28.670
John Wick: The End

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:33.240
As it stands, John Wick: Chapter 3 will be
the last movie that will focus on Reeves'

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.260
character, at least as far as the filmmakers
are concerned.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:40.470
Asked by The Independent if he saw the third
chapter as the final one, Chad Stahelski's

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.710
answer was yes, although he left the final
decision in the hands of Lionsgate.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:48.330
It seems like there’s a slim chance Reeves
could return in a fourth film, but it’s

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:53.460
more likely that the studio is planning on
doing more John Wick movies without the character.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.790
According to the Hollywood Reporter, Lionsgate
has already purchased a screenplay called

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:03.110
Ballerina, described as Luc Besson meets Quentin
Tarantino, with the intention of releasing

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.350
it as a John Wick spinoff.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:08.790
There's been little news of the project since,
which suggests that Lionsgate intend to see

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.990
the John Wick trilogy out before expanding
the universe.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:15.300
That doesn't mean that Keanu Reeves will never
play the character again, though.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:20.140
In January 2018, Starz, the television network
owned by Lionsgate, confirmed that it was

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:23.160
developing a TV series called The Continental.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.390
While it’s based on the hotel that Wick
and the other assassins frequent, it’s been

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:30.530
revealed that Reeves would not be the star,
but will still reprise the role for occasional

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.540
appearances.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:36.440
With Chapter 2 introducing an incredible number
of new characters and Chapter 3 set to possibly

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.690
involve a conflict between the Continental
and the High Table, there’s plenty to work

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:44.370
with in the wider John Wick universe… as
long as all the assassins know they should

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.360
stay away from everyone’s pets.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.400
Thanks for watching!

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.180
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:51.970
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

